-- v10 → v11 (MK.EPG.D): composite (type, tvg_id) index on `content`.
--
-- Every Guide query filters `type = 'live'` then either matches or
-- groups on `tvg_id`:
--   * guideChannelsAll/BySource/ByGroupPaged + count* counterparts —
--     `WHERE type='live' AND tvg_id IS NOT NULL ... GROUP BY tvg_id`
--   * selectLiveByTvgId — `WHERE type='live' AND tvg_id = ?` (catchup
--     resolution, hit on every catchup-launch click)
--   * distinctLiveTvgIds — feeds the EPG importer's keep-set; runs
--     before every periodic `EpgSyncWorker` tick (every 6h)
--   * distinctGuideGroups — chip strip on the Guide screen
--
-- With only `idx_content_type` the planner seeks to the `live` block
-- and then scans the full live row set per query. On a typical IPTV
-- catalog (5–20k live channels) every channel-list page does ~15k row
-- reads before the EXISTS subquery on `epg_programmes` runs. The
-- composite turns the `type='live' AND tvg_id ...` filter into a
-- direct seek and lets `GROUP BY c.tvg_id` consume rows in index
-- order — eliminating a sort step too.
--
-- Pure additive: no constraint or column changes, so existing rows
-- pick the index up on the next write/read without re-encoding.
-- Build cost is one-shot and proportional to live row count (a few
-- ms on a v9 DB with 20k channels).
CREATE INDEX idx_content_type_tvg ON content(type, tvg_id);
